description: Prove a fix with the failing path before saying it works
alwaysApply: true
---

# Verify before claiming a fix

Do not treat a code change as fixed because it compiles or because the new logic looks right.

- Read the live logs or the failing output first.
- Add or run a test that fails on the broken behavior and passes after the change.
- Run that test. If the bug is in a running app, build the checkout that actually launches and exercise that path.
- Say what was verified and what was not.
